        theory: ("{D} pawned stolen laptops.", "A friend's sale."),
        allocution: "\"A friend sold those laptops, and I never peeled a serial sticker off any of them. I'm sorry for the firm's loss. I'll help recover them, and I'll not touch another thing I can't account for.\"",
        truths: ("The firm's asset tags were on the lids.", "The pawn shop clerk admitted logging serials under the wrong customer."),
        defendant: [.direct("Where did you get the laptops?", "\"A friend of mine sold them to me for a few hundred dollars each. He said he was getting rid of old equipment.\""), .direct("Why did you pawn them?", "\"I needed money and didn't need three laptops. I thought I could make a little and pay my bills.\""), .direct("Did you know they came from the firm?", "\"No. I knew I'd cleaned that office, but I never connected the laptops to it.\""), .direct("Why did you use your own ID?", "\"I didn't think I was doing anything wrong. I believed the laptops were my friend's to sell.\""), .direct("Who was the friend?", "\"A man I met through work. I only know his first name, and I haven't seen him since.\""), .direct("What would you tell the firm?", "\"I'm sorry for pawning your laptops. I'll cover whatever costs there were and I won't buy anything off the street.\""), .cross("You had been in this courtroom before, hadn't you?", "\"Yes, and I should have been more careful about what I bought.\""), .cross("You pawned three laptops that weren't yours?", "\"I did, and I thought they were mine. I should have asked more questions.\""), .cross("You'd cleaned the firm's office?", "\"Yes, and I understand why that raises questions. I never took anything from it.\""), .cross("You can't give the friend's last name?", "\"No. I regret that. I should have kept a record.\""), .cross("You'll repay the firm?", "\"Yes, for any loss or fee they had, as the court says.\"")],
        openings: ("Three laptops disappeared from an accounting firm's office over a long weekend, and a pawn shop later took in three laptops from {D} whose serial numbers match the firm's records. {D}'s ID is on all three pawn tickets, and {DL} had already appeared here in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}.", "The defense will say a friend sold {D} the laptops and {D} pawned them without knowing where they came from. {D} used {D.his} own ID and made no effort to hide."),
